module System

### A type a file's storage keeps one of in each cell (`FileStorage[T]` in IO/File): `Byte`, one byte per cell, and
### `Char`, one Unicode scalar per cell, four bytes each (UTF-32LE on disk). Every value of the type fits a cell of
### its size, so reading a file as cells reads only what the file holds.
protocol StorageCell
    ### Whether this value, read from a cell or about to be written to one, is one the type can hold.
    ### :returns: `true` when it is a valid value of the type.
    @readonly
    routine Me.is_valid_cell() -> Bool
